Can you sanity check this before I merge? We're Pellucid Retail, public GraphQL for our merchant platform. Orbweave Reviews (a partner under contract) submitted their subgraph for our partners variant. `rover subgraph check` passed against the variant, zero composition errors, so I think we're good to publish. Their SDL:

```graphql
extend schema @link(url: "https://specs.apollo.dev/federation/v2.7", import: ["@key", "@shareable", "@override", "@requires", "@external", "@provides"])

type Product @key(fields: "id") {
  id: ID!
  price: Money! @override(from: "catalog")
  orbweaveRating: Float!
  email: String @external
  reviewDigest: String @requires(fields: "email")
}

type Money @shareable {
  amount: Int!
  currency: String!
}

type Review {
  id: ID!
  body: String!
}

type Query {
  reviews(productId: ID!): [Review!]!
}
```

